@startuml team-lead-reassignment
title Team lead gives a ticket to a technician of the team (ADR-045, Phase M3)

actor "Team lead" as Lead
participant "Team Lead tab\n(app.js)" as UI
participant "TechnicianController\nPOST /api/technician/incidents/{id}/reassign\n@PreAuthorize TEAM_LEAD" as Ctl
participant "TeamLeadReassignmentService\n(one transaction)" as Svc
participant "Incident\n(State Pattern)" as Inc
participant "Technician" as Tech
participant "AssignmentDecisionRecorder\n(MANDATORY)" as Rec
participant "DomainEventPublisher" as Pub

Lead -> UI : Assign / Reassign
UI -> Ctl : GET /api/admin/technicians (own team)\nGET /api/technician/incidents/{id}
Ctl --> UI : roster + ticket (reassignable = server flag)
Lead -> UI : pick technician + reason
UI -> Ctl : {technicianId, reason}
Ctl -> Svc : reassign(ticket, lead, technician, reason)
Svc -> Svc : reason present?\nlead.canReassignTeamTickets()\nAccessPolicy REASSIGN on the ticket\nnot in triage, status allows it
Svc -> Svc : target in the lead's own team,\nactive, not offline, not the holder
alt ticket held by a technician
  Svc -> Inc : flagWrongDomain (back to CLASSIFIED)
  Svc -> Tech : previous holder.releaseIncident
end
Svc -> Inc : assign(target)  [CLASSIFIED -> ASSIGNED]
Svc -> Tech : target.assignIncident  (full -> 409, all undone)
Svc -> Inc : addNote(internal: reason)
Svc -> Rec : recordManual(actor = lead)
Svc -> Pub : IncidentAssigned
Svc --> Ctl : saved ticket
Ctl --> UI : 200 TechnicianIncidentView
UI -> UI : close dialog, reload the open tab

note right of Svc
  Refusals: 403 not a lead / other team's ticket /
  other team's technician / ticket in triage;
  409 status not allowed, offline or full technician;
  404 unknown ticket or technician; 400 missing reason,
  same technician. Administrators only see the decision
  ("Why This Technician").
end note
@enduml
